    "created_at": "2019-04-22T09:17:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-22T09:17:42Z",
    "body": "If the semantics are that the browser does a copy, you'll probably force it to make a copy, just to be sure that racing writes that would not be observable under a copy model are not in fact observed.  What have we done elsewhere where we accept shared memory?",
